Hell no. Marcos thinks he has so much.

66
00:07:07.916 --> 00:07:11.750
- So. I'll keep him waiting. for now.
- Don't want to give the devil more power.

67
00:07:13.541 --> 00:07:15.208
- Don't you follow the news?
- What?

68
00:07:15.291 --> 00:07:18.500
Your flirtatious popcorn vendor
is one of the richest men in the country.

69
00:07:18.583 --> 00:07:21.125
- I know. he mentioned it.
- And?

70
00:07:21.208 --> 00:07:23.833
And he's never going to leave his wife.

71
00:07:23.916 --> 00:07:25.208
They have a daughter.

72
00:07:25.833 --> 00:07:28.833
You still haven't learned
that you won't find a husband here?

73
00:07:30.333 --> 00:07:32.458
- That man is a prince.
- What?

74
00:07:32.541 --> 00:07:34.125
He's not a vendor.

75
00:07:34.208 --> 00:07:35.708
He's the prince of popcorn.

76
00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:44.458
- Hey. Kelly!
- Huh?

77
00:07:44.541 --> 00:07:46.291
I was thinking…

78
00:07:46.375 --> 00:07:49.916
You know. you and my daughter
look very similar.

79
00:07:51.708 --> 00:07:53.000
Oh. thank you.

80
00:07:55.583 --> 00:07:58.416
- Night. Renan. Take care.
- Elize. Are you avoiding me?

81
00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.208
- Oh. no.
- I need to talk to you.

82
00:08:00.291 --> 00:08:02.458
- I don't want to talk to you.
- Don't be dramatic.

83
00:08:02.541 --> 00:08:04.458
I've been calling over and over.
You vanished.

84
00:08:04.541 --> 00:08:06.791
- I have a life.
- All this because I'm married?

85
00:08:06.875 --> 00:08:10.125
- I don't care. I can't anymore.
- I have a daughter. I know. I have a wife.

86
00:08:10.208 --> 00:08:11.041
Uh-huh. yeah.

87
00:08:11.125 --> 00:08:13.125
